# TASK-026 — eventlog replayer; sub-branch agent/a/m2-w2b-eventlog-replayer

## Cut-1 scope notes

- `eventlog.Replayer` implements both passthrough (synthetic-body / nil
  components) and proto-dispatch (real `*rtiv1.Event` body oneof routed
  through `core.FederationStore` and `core.ObjectRegistry`).
- Spec test `TestSpec_M2_Replay_ByteIdentical` is GREEN via passthrough
  (the orchestrator-supplied fixture builds a synthetic source).
- Spec test `TestSpec_M2_Replay_DivergenceIsFatal` REMAINS `t.Skip` —
  the orchestrator's scaffold owes a frozen-test update to wire the
  divergence-injection harness against the new
  `eventlog.ErrReplayDivergence` sentinel and the optional
  `ReplayerOptions.CapturedBuffer`. Flag this as a contract-change-
  request candidate post-merge. The internal package test
  `TestReplayer_Replay_DivergenceIsFatal` covers the same guarantee in
  `rti/internal/eventlog/replayer_test.go`.

## Header-byte caveat (M2 cut-1 stance)

Byte-equality is asserted from offset `HeaderSize` onward only. The
header `CreatedAtNs` field is by-construction a wall-clock recording at
`NewWriter` time and excluded from the determinism contract. Magic /
version / federation / mode / seed match by construction because the
replay harness wires the same `WriterOptions` into the captured Writer.

## Coverage

- `rti/internal/eventlog/...` total: 90.9% (covers writer, reader,
  replayer, format, doc).
- `replayer.go`: NewReplayer 100%, Replay 100%, dispatch/dispatch
  branches 71-100% (uncovered branches are defensive: non-eventRecord
  source, unknown body type — both unreachable from production).
